What is Decarbonized Concrete?
Decarbonized concrete is an innovative construction material engineered to dramatically lower CO₂ emissions associated with traditional Portland cement production. The material achieves its low‑carbon footprint through a combination of strategies: integrating low‑carbon raw materials (such as fly ash, slag, limestone, and calcined clays), employing CO₂ mineralization and solidification techniques, substituting clinker with supplementary cementitious materials, and in some cases, developing cement‑free geopolymer binders or biologically derived alternatives. These approaches not only cut the embodied carbon of new structures but also endorse circular‑economy principles while preserving structural performance, durability, and compliance with existing building codes.
